 "intro_html": "Cook the rice on its own. Tender-cook all the octopus separately, drain and dry it, then brown and glaze it briefly. Fold only the coated pieces and green onion into the cooked rice. This keeps the rice texture under control and avoids cooking it in purple octopus liquor; a little local colour from the glaze is normal. This is a home adaptation, rather than traditional takomeshi (rice cooked with octopus).",
