    {
     "amount_html": "about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"300\">300 g</span> (10–12)",
     "name_html": "Baby octopus (iidako)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wash the rice until the water runs nearly clear, drain well, then soak in the measured <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"300\" data-s=\"0\">300 ml</span> fresh water for 20 minutes. Keep that water for cooking.</li><li>Slice ginger into thin matchsticks, then cut across them and finely chop to <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"mm\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 mm</span>. Reserve for the pan; no long fibres in the filling.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wash rice; finely chop ginger",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [],
