    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"300\">300 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water for rice"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cover all the chopped octopus with fresh water in a saucepan. Bring to a gentle simmer and cook quietly; start checking after 20 minutes.</li><li>Cool a piece and taste it. Continue in 5–10 minute intervals until it bites easily; size and species change the timing. Pink and opaque alone is not enough.</li><li>Drain and discard all cooking liquor. Spread on clean towels and pat thoroughly dry. If using already tender-cooked octopus, skip the simmer and dry it well.</li></ul>",
