  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lower the heat. Stir the finely chopped ginger in the remaining oil for 20–30 seconds. Add soy, mirin, sugar and <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span> water.</li><li>Bubble gently for 1–2 minutes until lightly syrupy. Return the browned octopus and toss for 30–60 seconds, just until a thin caramelized sweet-soy coating clings. Stop before sugar burns.</li><li>Lift the coated pieces out with tongs or a slotted spoon. Leave any excess sauce in the pan.</li></ul>",
